@Software Architect and @DevOps Specialist: I strongly support the proposed DLQ pattern and robust resource mapping (*Observation*, *DiagnosticReport*, *ServiceRequest*). 

From a Product Owner perspective, unmappable payloads in the DLQ represent potential lost lab results that directly threaten patient safety. We must establish a business process and a lightweight administrative dashboard view so compliance or clinical operations teams can review, correct, and re-inject DLQ messages rather than leaving them trapped in technical logs. 

Additionally, to satisfy modern interoperability mandates and third-party patient app ecosystems (such as Apple Health Records), I propose we ensure our SMART-on-FHIR implementation fully supports patient-access scopes alongside clinician scopes, directly empowering patients to retrieve their own clinical data.
